SUMMARY:Duke Forest Figure Eight Hike
DESCRIPTION:Triangle Hiking and Outdoors Group\nWe will start at Gate 26 o
 n Whitfield Road (see map and How to Find Us). We will hike down to New Ho
 pe Creek and follow the south side of the creek to the NEW Bridge. We will
  cross and continue on the Concrete Bridge Trail\, the Wooden Bridge Trail
  and then along New Hope Creek back to the new bridge. We will cross it an
 d continue on Concrete Bridge FT to the Gate 25 to Gate 26 connector and r
 eturn to the cars.\n\nThe hike is about 6.5 miles long. Half is on fire tr
 ails (= multiuse trails) and hilly but easy. The part along New Hope Creek
  is rocky and rooty with scrambling over rocks.\n\nWe will maintain a pace
  of about 3 miles per hour and take short breaks as needed. Bring water an
 d snacks.\n\nBy participating in this event\, you agree to the terms below
 :\n\nTRIP PARTICIPANT WAIVER OF LIABILITY I fully realize that this activi
 ty involves a risk of personal injury\, property damage\, or loss of my pe
 rson or property. I hereby for myself\, my heirs\, executors and administr
 ators\, and same for persons with whom are in my party\, waive and release
  any claims or rights against Triangle Hiking & Outdoors Group (THOG)\, al
 l of its owners and coordinators for any and all injury\, damages or loss 
 to my person or property incurred during this activity. I also understand 
 that THOG organizers are not required\, nor should it be assumed that they
  are CPR/First Aid/Wilderness Survival Certified and I am responsible for 
 my own personal safety.
